{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3058","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3058","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3058\",\"parent_revision\":\"659ea8e743c6c4b2d0479b586ffc48f181dbb8da\",\"root_revision\":\"6c082d43c12da2a5c134c1693a20df7e41baa6c180ea6b3a7e3003083d208713\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPlan reads, task reads, and artifact content reads return whole documents with no size guard. Harnesses commonly cap a single tool response near 10,000 tokens. Artifacts can be full architecture specifications or codebase analyses; a ready-task listing returns every task body at once.\\n\\nExisting plan and task documentation is silent on content size \u2014 it does not acknowledge that large plans or tasks exist.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-20T10:08:28.927871Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: refactor: route plan, task, and artifact reads through the markdown engine\\nDate: 2026-09-20\\nGoal: Every plan read, task read, artifact content read, and ready-task listing returns a usable response within the token budget, with the whole of a large document reachable across successive calls.\\nConditions:\\n1. The affected read surfaces are identified with their locations | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Whether any of the four surfaces applies a token budget today | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. The budget constant to apply, and how it resolves | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. The normative behaviour required of an over-budget response | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Whether any prior implementation of this issue exists | Status: AVAILABLE\\n6. Output-schema headroom available for new response fields | Status: AVAILABLE\\n7. Which existing callers consume the four surfaces and would see a changed response shape | Status: DERIVABLE\\n8. What the plan and task documentation currently says about content size | Status: DERIVABLE\\n9. Whether the engine's navigator can address a structured plan or task record, or only free markdown | Status: DERIVABLE\\n10. Whether a ready-task listing's size is bounded by task count, document size, or both | Status: DERIVABLE\\n11. The scope boundary between this issue and #3078 for artifact content reads | Status: MISSING\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 4\\nMISSING count: 1\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\nNotes on the conditions, with evidence, verified on 7e6381259:\\n\\n1. Four surfaces: sam_plan (sam_schema/server.py:95), sam_task (sam_schema/server.py:167), artifact_read (backlog_core/server.py:3522), backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks (backlog_core/server.py:3606).\\n2. None. sam_schema/server.py contains no token-budget constant. backlog_view and backlog_list apply their own; these four do not.\\n3. _DEFAULT_BUDGET at progressive_markdown/models.py:15, resolving to MAX_MCP_OUTPUT_TOKENS - 500, falling back to 9,500. R2 requires the budget to come from one constant.\\n4. docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md. R2 forbids dropping, eliding or truncating any addressable node to fit a budget. R3 requires the compact form to be returned automatically, with no caller opt-in.\\n5. No prior implementation. PR #3551's description lists #3058 among the issues still tracking this work.\\n6. backlog_view's own schema measures 1,706 tokens against a 2,000 ceiling. The total across all tools measures 12,773 against the 13,000 ceiling in tests/test_tool_output_schemas.py, leaving 227 tokens. The total is the binding constraint.\\n11. This is the one condition a tool cannot settle. #3058 covers \\\"artifact content reads\\\". #3078 is titled \\\"artifact content delivery bypasses the markdown engine entirely\\\" and states that artifact_read() returns raw content with no parsing, navigation or pagination. Both appear to own the same surface. Either #3078 is a subset of this issue, or one of the two drops artifact reads from its scope. Two plans touching artifact_read would collide the way #3057 and #3059 do on disclosure_handler.py. The owner decides.\\n\\nThis is the pre-swarm baseline. The rtica-assessor's final pass in finalize.md supersedes it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Plan read, task read, and artifact content read route through the markdown engine\\n- [ ] Each returns the compact form automatically when over budget, per R3\\n- [ ] A listing operation does not embed unbounded bodies\\n- [ ] No response can exceed the configured budget regardless of stored document size\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P0 \u2014 unbounded responses against a hard harness cap fail rather than degrade\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"63384b8cab7fc8234d2d6ffabc3066d04b5ab0e032b4339990cb0089a79fc845\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVqzzTQ\"}"}